# L1_2 (Cu3Au-type) ordering target on FCC 3x3x3 = 108 atoms.
# Species: 0 = A (3 face-centers), 1 = B (corners).
#
# In L1_2 each B atom has 12 NN, all A. So:
#   shell 0 (NN, z=12): alpha_AB = 1 - P(B|A)/c_B = 1 - (1/3)/0.25 = -1/3
#                       alpha_BA = 1 - P(A|B)/c_A = 1 - 1/0.75 = -1/3
#   shell 1 (2NN, z=6): A's and B's 2NN are all same species (sublattice
#                       offset places them on same sublattice line).
#                       alpha_AB = 1 - 0/0.25 = +1
SRO 0 1 0 -0.333333
SRO 0 1 1 +1.0
